On Tue, Jul 7, 2009 at 10:58 PM, Chris Capel<pdf23ds@gmail.com> wrote:
> "abu ta'e sezystidi lo'e xamgu mutce to ku'i ta'enai mapti zukte toi
> gi'e su'oroi tai junri sezytolzarsku ja'e lo'e nu gasnu le nu le se
> klaku cu zvati le kanla"
>
> The problem is with "su'oroi", which doesn't work directly after a
> gihek unless it's followed by a bo.

Not exactly. "su'oroi" is not meant as a connective here, it's meant
to tag the following selbri. "gi'e su'oroi junri sezytolzarsku" would
be fine. The problem is that the official grammar doesn't allow
"su'oroi tai" as a compound tag.

See:
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Internal+grammar+of+tags
for a proposal that would make both this and "ka'e nai" grammatical.

